        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Is the Redliro under desk treadmill worth buying?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              It can be, for slow walking at a desk on a tight budget. It is light, low and inexpensive. The caveats are that its listings disagree on capacity, speed and weight between models, its motor rating has no stated basis, and Redliro's warranty is one year. Check the exact listing, buy near the bottom of the price range, and read the seller's return policy first.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the weight limit on a Redliro walking pad?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              It depends on the model. Current under-desk listings claim 265 lb, the older Redliro 2-in-1 is rated at 220 lb, and a wood-finish model is listed at 300 lb. These are listing claims on light machines; leave a generous margin, and use the figure on the listing you are buying from, not a review of a different model.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How fast does the Redliro under desk treadmill go?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Current flat Redliro pads are listed at 0.5 to 4 mph by remote. The older Redliro 2-in-1 is listed at up to 7.5 mph with its handrail raised and 4 mph with it folded down. Either way, the short, narrow belt makes it a walking machine rather than a running one.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does Redliro still sell under-desk treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Not on its own website. On 14 October 2026 redliro.com listed four handrail walking treadmills for older adults and no flat under-desk pad. Redliro under-desk pads were still listed by marketplace sellers on sites including Best Buy and Walmart, so you would be buying through a marketplace.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What warranty does Redliro offer?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              One year from the original purchase date, for the original purchaser and residential indoor use, on products bought from Redliro or authorised resellers it names as Amazon, Walmart, Target and TikTok. Redliro may send parts, replace the product or refund it, at its discretion, and asks you to activate the warranty online after ordering.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is the Redliro walking pad quiet?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The sources disagree. TODAY's 2026 tester found the Redliro Mini Walking Pad louder than expected, while Treadmill Review Guru found the older 2-in-1's motor quiet. On any walking pad, footfall into the floor is often louder than the motor. Try it at your real walking speed inside the return window if noise matters.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
            machine has not been tested hands-on, and we never accept payment for a placement. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Read our review process.</a>
          </p>
